WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:06.480
2017 was filled with cinematic wins, from
horror hits like Get Out and It to the continued

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.440
superhero domination of Logan, Wonder Woman
and Thor: Ragnarok to indie favorites like

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.260
Baby Driver and The Big Sick.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.760
But not every movie that made way to the silver
screen this year has seen such success.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.520
Here are just some of the biggest stinkers
Hollywood produced in 2017.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.240
The Book of Henry

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.119
After the positive critical reception of Safety
Not Guaranteed and the financial success of

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:32.870
Jurassic World, director Colin Trevorrow made
a serious misstep with The Book of Henry.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:38.070
Sure, his third feature has a fantastic poster,
but the film itself was widely dissed and

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:38.620
dismissed.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.860
The pic stars It's Jaeden Lieberher as the
title character, an insanely intelligent 11-year-old

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:48.540
who spends his days inventing Rube Goldberg
machines, investing in the stock market, and

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.300
taking care of his adorable brother.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.800
Henry is so smart as to be obnoxious—constantly
correcting every adult around him, from doctors

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.160
to school principals.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.160
"Hank."

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.540
It's actually Henry.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.560
I'd think you'd be able to retain one single
name somewhere beyond that haircut."

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.680
This prompted critics to pan the would-be
hero as smug and unlikable, even as he tries

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.680
to rescue his neighbor from being abused by
her police commissioner stepdad by way of

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.440
an elaborate assassination plot.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.480
Once his own life reaches the point of peril,
it's hard to care about him anymore.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.760
Wish Upon

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.760
When Wish Upon hit theaters in July, it faced
some steep box office competition from War

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.180
for the Planet of the Apes, but that was the
least of this film's problems.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.780
Instead, it was the movie's ridiculous plotline
that sunk any interest in the film.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.890
It followed a high school outcast named Clare
who comes into possession of a mysterious

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.540
box that's been possessed by a demon who'll
grant her wishes but takes a life in return

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.800
for her heart's desires.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.200
While the obvious way to beat this box is
to simply stop wishing, Clare just can't get

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.540
enough, and keeps wishing for things that
are hardly worth the cost.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.220
Critics hated the derivative plot and its
superficial centerpiece, and the film barely

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.900
recouped its modest budget.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.140
The House

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.080
You can hire all the comedians you want, but
if you don't have a solid script, then your

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.360
movie won't get any laughs.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.479
That was the problem with The House, the latest
from Andrew Jay Cohen and Brendan O'Brien

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.480
of Neighbors and Mike and Dave Need Wedding
Dates fame.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.930
Although The House boasts the talents of Will
Ferrell and Amy Poehler, instead of giving

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:17.740
them a strong screenplay to work with …

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.720
"Which we were kinda counting on…"

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.200
It leans almost exclusively on their improv
skills.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.610
The so-called "comedy" revolves around a pair
of parents who open a casino in their friend's

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.060
house to raise tuition money for their daughter,
but things get wildly out of control.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.360
Soon, the two become suburbanite mobsters,
using drugs and chopping off fingers.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:40.360
While it seems like this wacky premise could
lead to some good gags, most of the jokes

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:44.540
failed to land with critics or those few audience
members who bothered to watch.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.940
A Family Man

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.930
Gerard Butler has not had a good year, thanks
in part to this movie.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.100
The plot for A Family Man follows his ruthless
businessman character who ignores his poor

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.739
children as he tries to win the favor of his
out-going employer and outmaneuver his office

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.280
rival to become the new boss, all while drinking
a lot of Red Bull.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.260
Of course, things get complicated when his
kid is diagnosed with leukemia, forcing our

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.220
hero to choose between his son and his job.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:14.040
All in all, A Family Man is a predictable
story that tries to jerk a few tears as Gerard

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.600
Butler becomes a good dad, but critics found
it hard to relate to or root for his character.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.240
The Emoji Movie

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.700
You might think a movie featuring Patrick
Stewart as a walking, talking piece of poop

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:29.090
would at least be worth watching as a gag,
but The Emoji Movie is such a soulless slog

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.290
it deprives you of even that simple pleasure.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:35.450
It's a movie that's supposedly about being
true to yourself, but really, it's just a

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.959
big commercial for Spotify and Candy Crush.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:42.340
A lot of people scoffed at the idea of this
movie when it was first announced, and rightfully

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:42.840
so.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.099
The film was obliterated by critics, even
though it still turned a profit at the box

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:47.640
office.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.080
The Last Face

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.780
There's no denying Sean Penn is a talented
filmmaker, but even the very best directors

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.320
come up with a bomb now and then.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:04:00.160
Unfortunately, The Last Face is so bad that
when it played at Cannes, the audience started

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.840
heckling the movie pretty much as soon as
it started rolling.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:08.180
The Last Face takes place in countries like
Sierra Leone, Liberia, and Sudan, but for

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:12.820
a film set in Africa, it's kind of weird that
all the black people are relegated to playing

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.320
background roles or mutilated corpses.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:19.940
Instead, the movie centers on beautiful white
people falling in love, which did not play

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.340
well to its audiences at the festival or earn
wide release as a result.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:26.040
The Nut Job 2: Nutty by Nature

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.120
The Nut Job wasn't exactly what you'd call
a masterpiece, but it made enough money to

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.060
prompt a sequel.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.500
Nutty by Nature follows its woodland stars
after they're forced to return to the wild,

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.940
at which point our furry friends—led by
Surly —move into the local city park.

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:44.659
Unfortunately, the mayor plans on chopping
down the trees and turning the area into a

00:04:44.659 --> 00:04:49.470
theme park—and he hires a group of exterminators
to deal with the rodents, forcing the critters

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.280
to fight back.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:54.760
Critics panned the pic for being boring and
unimaginative, and it earned less than half

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.920
the revenue of its predecessor due to audience
disinterest.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.520
The Dark Tower

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:04.360
Hollywood has tried to adapt Stephen King's
Dark Tower series for years—and now, after

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.940
years of waiting, fans of the novels can finally
see Roland shoot with his mind on the big

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:09.440
screen.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.380
Unfortunately, the movie was absolutely awful
and failed to capture any of the magic that

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.760
made the books so beloved.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.740
The Dark Tower stars Idris Elba as a gunslinger
dedicated to protecting the titular tower

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.140
and defending 11-year-old Jake from the Man
in Black.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:27.699
Dark Tower should've been a slam dunk, but
instead of being as original and exhilarating

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:32.590
as the books, the movie was derided as generic
action fare, which is everything King's version

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.240
was not.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:34.960
Flatliners

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.540
When the original Flatliners hit theaters
back in 1990, it made a pretty penny at the

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.720
box office, but still failed to impress many
critics.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.319
Compared to this year's pseudo-sequel, though,
the original feels like an absolute masterpiece

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:47.940
of horror.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.200
The film follows a group of med students experimenting
with life after life.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:56.639
Their tests involve taking some heavy duty
drugs, stopping their hearts for a minute

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.040
or two, and checking out the other side before
being resuscitated.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:04.830
Naturally, messing around with the afterlife
has serious consequences, but when our heroes

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:09.800
start experiencing some "spooky" visions,
the film devolves into Jump Scare: The Movie.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.520
Critics called out the film's lack of suspense,
foolish characters, and lacking visuals, leading

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.040
many to wish the property would've just stayed
dead.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:19.420
Geostorm

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:24.720
When the trailer for Geostorm first hit, everybody
knew we were in for something brainless, but

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:27.340
audiences had their fingers crossed for some
campy fun.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:32.400
Unfortunately, the film had almost no redeeming
qualities and got laughed out of the theaters.

00:06:32.409 --> 00:06:36.300
The film followed a man trying to save a series
of satellites that protect the world from

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.080
apocalyptic weather events after somebody
sabotages the system.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.900
With catastrophes breaking out across the
globe, there's a lot of visual flair in play,

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:50.480
but those action scenes are few and far between,
interrupted by long segments of boring, flat

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.960
characters staring at a bunch of screens.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.460
The Snowman

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.320
On paper, The Snowman should've been awesome.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:01.940
It stars several formidable thespians and
was directed by Tomas Alfredson, director

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.760
of Let the Right One In and Tinker, Tailor,
Soldier, Spy.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:08.080
But despite all that talent, this film is
a bloody mess.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:12.700
Based on the novel by Jo Nesbø, The Snowman
follows an alcoholic detective who chases

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.860
a psycho with a thing for building snowmen.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:20.240
Unfortunately, the thrills are undone by a
slew of messy subplots, over-the-top music,

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.440
subpar performances, and a bunch of supposedly
freaky Frostys that really aren't that frightening.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:30.080
It also didn't help that The Snowman had one
of the worst—and most meme-worthy—marketing

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.659
campaigns in recent Hollywood history.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:33.360
"You could've saved them.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.260
I gave you all the clues."

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:40.500
Instead of being scary, the movie ended up
arriving as one of the year's most unintentionally

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.020
funny movies … but only after being ... plowed
by critics.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:44.640
Get it?

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:46.040
Jeez.. that's as bad as the movie..

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.480
Thanks for watching.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:51.880
Click the link for the rest of 2017s worst movies and check out all this other stuff

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:52.769
we know you'll love too

